<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Is it compliant to charge a consultation fee at a DHA-licensed clinic?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A booking-logistics fee that secures an appointment time and is credited toward treatment is an administrative charge, not a medical claim or promotion, and is standard practice at well-run clinics. Always verify current requirements with the Dubai Health Authority (DHA) or your licensing consultant before rolling out a new policy."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What's a reasonable no-show rate for a UAE aesthetic clinic?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Clinics with a deposit and reminder system in place typically see no-show rates in the low single digits. Clinics with no system at all often run considerably higher without realising it."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I mention a patient's original appointment when offering their slot to someone on the waitlist?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No — the waitlist message to a new patient should only reference the new availability itself, never why the slot opened or any detail about the original patient's booking."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Should reminder messages mention treatment pricing?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Keep reminders focused on appointment logistics rather than treatment pricing or claims, which belong in compliant marketing materials, not a booking reminder."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How is this different from what a salon does to reduce no-shows?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The mechanics are the same, but clinic communication needs to stay administrative and confidential rather than casual or promotional."}}]}</script>

			
			
